// LANGUAGE_GAPS.md #7: the simple, straight-line, non-escaping case -
// checked against the PRE-optimization IR directly (see this item's own
// commit/LANGUAGE_GAPS.md notes on why: LLVM's own optimizer aggressively
// eliminates a malloc'd block it can prove never escapes a function,
// REGARDLESS of whether this pass's own free() is present or correct -
// runtime memory measurement can't distinguish "my code freed it" from
// "the optimizer deleted the whole allocation as dead code" once
// optimized, so this is verified against output_pre_opt.ll instead,
// which reflects exactly what THIS pass emitted, unclouded by later
// optimization). Hand-predicted: 5 (the drop itself doesn't affect this
// value - the point of this program is to give the compiler something
// real to emit codegen for; the IR inspection below is the actual check).
struct Blob {
    a: i64,
    b: i64
}

fn main() -> i64 = {
    let blob: Blob = own Blob { a: 5, b: 6 };
    blob.a
}
